  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 41\u2011year\u2011old man with a long\u2011standing history of type 2 diabetes mellitus complicated by progressive diabetic kidney disease. Kidney function declined from CKD stage\u202f1 in 1995 to stage\u202f4 by 2004, accompanied by microalbuminuria, proteinuria, and anemia. He also has non\u2011proliferative diabetic retinopathy and peripheral neuropathy. Lifestyle factors include daily tobacco use, chronic alcohol use, and opioid abuse, all documented since the early 1990s. He is currently awaiting kidney transplantation. Current medication list is limited to insulin, vitamin\u202fB12, and a nicotine patch; guideline\u2011directed therapies for CKD (ACE\u2011I/ARB, statin, erythropoietin, antihypertensives) are absent. Recent labs show an A1c of 4.0\u202f% (normal), but blood pressure, eGFR, and lipid panels are missing. The overall trajectory reflects worsening renal function, high cardiovascular risk, and significant psychosocial challenges.",
